\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Thee will I love, my strength for ever;
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 Thee will I love, Thou art my grace!
\par Thee will I love in all endeavour,
\par Thro' all temptations which I face.
\par Thee will I love, my light Thou art,
\par Till breaks my yearning heart.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. Ah, that so late I got to know Thee,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 exalted, wondrous beauty, Thou!
\par That I not sooner did confess Thee
\par and found Thy true rest only now
\par This is my deep regret and grief,
\par so late I found relief.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I ran astray in deep confusion;
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj I searched, but no where could Thee sight.
\par I turned from Thee in my delusion
\par and loved the garish worldly light
\par But now through Thee it's been achieved,
\par Thy love I have perceived!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I give Thee thanks, Thou true sun given,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj that light to me Thy splendor brought.
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 I give Thee thanks, Thou bliss from heaven,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj Who for me joy and freedom wrought.
\par I give Thee thanks, O word so pure,
\par That Thou my ills doth cure.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thee will l  love, my crown O Thou art,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 Thee will I love, my Lord, my God
\par Thee will I love with, all of my heart
\par in times of joy or painful lot.
\par Thee will I love, my crown Thou art,
\par \pard   Till breaks my yearning heart.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

